From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:33:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(design): the design system as W3C tokens, compiled
 to CSS, with shared component styles

Adds @yukibana/design: the tokens the design rounds settled (cool greys, Light's green as the one accent, type, radii,
focus, motion), in the W3C Design Tokens format with a dark override file; a compiler to `--yk-*` custom properties with
`light-dark()`; the shared `yk-` component styles (buttons, chips, fields, drawn checkboxes, callouts, page and dock
tabs, Expressive Code frames, messages, skeleton, empty state, lattice, header, tables); and a reference page.

The tests check that the committed CSS is what the tokens compile to, and that every text pair passes 4.5:1 and every
control 3:1 in both themes. No app uses the package yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
